   $q$Read the sentence: "The engineer ___ designed the new footbridge spoke to our physics class." Which choice correctly completes the relative clause?$q$, $q$[{"text":"whose","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"possessive-pronoun-misused"},{"text":"whom","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"object-pronoun-as-subject"},{"text":"which","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"which-for-person"},{"text":"who","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$who$q$, $q$The relative pronoun is the subject of "designed" and refers to a person, so "who" is correct. "Whom" is used only as an object, and "which" refers to things.$q$, 'draft', null)
