   $q$Read the sentence: "Climbing the ladder, the paint can tipped over." Which revision fixes the misused participial phrase?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Climbing the ladder, Dmitri tipped over the paint can.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The paint can, climbing the ladder, tipped over.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"dangling-modifier-remains"},{"text":"Climbing the ladder the paint can tipped over.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"punctuation-only-fix"},{"text":"Climbing the ladder, the paint can was tipped over.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"dangling-modifier-remains"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Climbing the ladder, Dmitri tipped over the paint can.$q$, $q$A participial phrase must describe the noun right after it, and only a person can climb a ladder, so "Dmitri" must follow the phrase. Making the verb passive still leaves the paint can doing the climbing.$q$, 'draft', null)
