   $q$Which choice is a complete sentence with an independent clause?$q$, $q$[{"text":"After the storm passed, the hikers returned to camp.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Returning to camp after the storm passed.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"fragment-participial-phrase"},{"text":"The hikers, who returned to camp after the storm passed.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"fragment-relative-clause"},{"text":"After the storm passed and the hikers returned to camp.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"fragment-dependent-clause"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$After the storm passed, the hikers returned to camp.$q$, $q$"The hikers returned to camp" is an independent clause, and "After the storm passed" is attached to it, so the sentence is complete. The version with "who" never gives "the hikers" a main verb, so it is a fragment.$q$, 'draft', null)
