   $q$Read the sentence: "The park ranger explained that the bison had moved north for fresh grass." What job does the noun clause "that the bison had moved north for fresh grass" do?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It describes \"ranger\" like an adjective.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-noun-relative"},{"text":"It is the direct object of \"explained.\"","is_correct":true},{"text":"It tells when the ranger spoke, like an adverb.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-noun-adverbial"},{"text":"It is the subject of the sentence.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-noun-clause-role"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It is the direct object of "explained."$q$, $q$The clause answers "explained what?", so it is the direct object of the verb "explained." The subject of the sentence is "the park ranger," not the clause.$q$, 'draft', null)
