   $q$Read the sentence: "To earn a lifeguard certificate, Keanu swam laps every morning." What job does the phrase "To earn a lifeguard certificate" do?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It describes the laps, acting as an adjective.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-adverbial-adjectival"},{"text":"It tells why Keanu swam laps, acting as an adverb.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It is an independent clause that could stand alone.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"phrase-called-clause"},{"text":"It names what Keanu swam, acting as a noun.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-adverbial-noun"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It tells why Keanu swam laps, acting as an adverb.$q$, $q$The infinitive phrase explains the purpose of swimming laps, so it acts as an adverb answering "why?" It has no subject of its own, so it is not a clause.$q$, 'draft', null)
